-- BIR: the six comparison operators of language.md §6.5 are method calls
-- carrying the operator they were written as (§1.3, §3.1): `==` and `/=`
-- ask for `eq`, `<` `<=` `>` `>=` ask for `compare`, and none of them
-- references `Basics` any more — the `refs` section is empty where
-- `import_value Basics.eq` used to stand. Their parenthesised forms are a
-- lambda over the same node (§3.1, Appendix A.22), not a reference to
-- `Basics.eq`, which would be structural equality and the wrong answer;
-- `(+)` beside them is unchanged.
comparisons a b =
    ( a == b, a /= b, a < b, a > b, a <= b, a >= b )


asFunctions =
    [ (==), (/=), (<), (>), (<=), (>=), (+) ]
